      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Mitosis is the process where one parent cell divides into two identical daughter cells. This vital process ensures that specialized body cells can grow, repair, and replace old cells. It involves distinct phases—Prophase, Metaphase, Anaphase, and Telophase—each with a specific role in separating the chromosomes accurately. Ultimately, mitosis allows for proper cell multiplication within a living organism.",
