      "content": "To best help students truly understand this, consider these detailed mechanics. In Prophase, DNA coils tightly into visible chromosomes, which is the first step to learn about genetic material location. Metaphase requires students to learn how these structures line up precisely at the cell's equator. Anaphase involves the separation of these chromatids, teaching students about exact chromosome movement. Telophase concludes with the formation of two new nuclei, followed by cytokinesis, where the cell membrane actually divides to create two independent, healthy daughter cells.",
